article_content:
Quick Answer: To edit a video with AI in Adobe Premiere, import your footage, generate a transcript, and cut the video by deleting words from the transcribed text. You can then clean up your audio with Enhance Audio and dynamic auto-ducking, automatically add captions, reframe footage for vertical and square formats with Auto Reframe, and lengthen clips with Generative Extend. Premiere on desktop and mobile exports videos without watermarks and is licensed for commercial use. Whether you’re a YouTuber, a digital marketer, or a creative pro, you likely know that shooting footage is the easy part. Editing your raw footage into a video that looks and sounds good, and keeps people’s attention, is the heavy lift. This is where the latest Beta version of Adobe Premiere steps up. Named a PCMag Best of the Year product in 2025, Premiere has a suite of baked-in (and recently refreshed) AI tools that automate basic, time-consuming tasks—transcribing, refining, cutting silences, coloring, and captioning, among others—freeing you up to focus on your narrative.Here’s how Premiere’s AI tools can supercharge your editing workflow from your desktop or phone, plus export commercial-grade content to your platform of choice.How Do You Edit a Video With AI in Adobe Premiere?

.pp-compare { margin: 1.5em 0; font-family: inherit; color: inherit; }

.pp-compare__scroll { overflow-x: auto; -webkit-overflow-scrolling: touch; }

.pp-compare table { width: 100%; min-width: 560px; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 0.95em; line-height: 1.45; }

.pp-compare caption { caption-side: top; text-align: left; font-weight: 700; font-size: 1.1em; padding: 0 0 0.6em; }

.pp-compare th, .pp-compare td { padding: 0.75em 1em; border-bottom: 1px solid #d9d9d9; text-align: center; vertical-align: top; }

.pp-compare thead th { background: #1a1a1a; color: #ffffff; font-weight: 700; border-bottom: none; }

.pp-compare tbody th { text-align: left; font-weight: 600; width: 28%; }

.pp-compare tbody tr:nth-child(even) { background: #f5f5f5; }

.pp-compare .pp-note { display: block; margin-top: 0.3em; font-size: 0.88em; opacity: 0.8; }

